{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Python integration: use stdin/stdout child-process approach (JPype/JNI rejected due to portability, GIL, and native library complexity); aligns with Spring XD's stream-based processing model.",
    "R integration: use Renjin (pure-JVM R interpreter) as the primary approach; rJava kept as a fallback if performance requires native execution.",
    "Hive sink: implement via HiveServer2 JDBC with batch-oriented writes, delegating HDFS concerns to the driver; use the existing Spring XD sink module SPI for consistency with other sinks.",
    "Spring Core 4.1.1 upgrade: treat the milestone as a drop-in replacement, but plan for SpEL compilation option enablement and minor API adjustments in the XD container and admin modules.",
    "Security model: build on Spring Security; introduce a security definitions registry mapped to entity identifiers (stream/job/tap), with group/role-based access expressions, and pluggable ACL evaluators shared by the DSL shell and Admin UI.",
    "ACL enforcement: centralize permission checks in a single AuthorizationService so DSL shell and Admin UI share semantics; defaults remain permissive (all) when ACLs are unconfigured.",
    "Testing: include unit tests per module plus integration tests that exercise end-to-end stream paths for processors/sinks and command paths for ACLs; Hive/Python/R tests marked as environment-dependent.",
    "Documentation: produce per-feature reference docs (SSL/Basic auth, Python processor, R processor, Hive sink, security model/ACLs) following the existing XD documentation format."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One developer performs all work; a standard workday equals 8 hours.",
    "The Spring XD runtime, build system, and a local single-node Hadoop/Hive test environment are pre-provisioned.",
    "Python 3 and R are available on the build/test nodes; no work is required to obtain or install them.",
    "The Spring 4.1.1 milestone artifacts are reachable from a configured repository and no upstream Spring issues block the upgrade.",
    "No production hardening, performance benchmarking, or large-scale cluster testing is included beyond smoke-level integration tests.",
    "Translation/localization of the Admin UI is out of scope; only English UI strings are touched.",
    "Migration tooling for upgrading existing deployments to use the new security/ACL features is not included."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Document SSL/HTTPS and Basic Authentication options (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Research the existing admin-endpoint configuration surface, identify all relevant properties (server.ssl.*, security.basic.*, management port), and write reference documentation with example configurations covering enabling, disabling, and combined SSL+Basic auth scenarios."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Python processor module (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Spike on integration approaches, design the PythonProcessor module API (input/output payload contract over stdio), implement the Java side that spawns the Python child process, handle process lifecycle, error streams, and back-pressure; provide unit tests, integration tests with a sample Python script, and user documentation."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement R processor module (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Spike on Renjin vs rJava trade-offs, design the RProcessor module API mirroring the Python one, embed Renjin to evaluate R expressions/scripts per tuple, integrate with the streaming pipeline, add unit/integration tests, and document the supported R API surface."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Hive sink module (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a HiveSink that writes batches of tuples to a configured Hive table via HiveServer2 JDBC, with table/partition options, connection pooling, and error handling; cover unit tests, integration tests against a local Hive instance, and documentation with example stream definitions."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Upgrade Spring Core to 4.1.1 milestone (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Bump the Spring dependency version in the build, audit and fix compilation/test failures introduced by the milestone, enable the compiled SpEL option where appropriate, and verify that all existing XD modules still function via the full test suite."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement entity-level security definitions (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Design a security-definitions model (name, entity type, group/role policies), expose it via configuration and an in-memory API, integrate with Spring Security for expression-based access control, implement evaluation utilities, and provide unit tests, integration tests, and reference documentation."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement DSL Shell ACL enforcement (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Introduce ACL configuration for shell-accessible resources (stream create/destroy/view, etc.), wire the AuthorizationService into the shell command handlers, add configuration parsing, defaults, unit tests, integration tests through the shell, and user documentation."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Implement Admin UI ACL enforcement (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Mirror the shell ACL model in the Admin UI, gate REST endpoints and UI actions through the same AuthorizationService, adjust UI to hide/disable disallowed operations, add unit/integration tests covering both allowed and denied paths, and document the configuration model."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Project setup, cross-module integration, and release prep",
      "activity_description": "Initial module scaffolding, dependency wiring, a final end-to-end integration test pass across the new processors/sink and security features, and preparation of release notes covering all user stories in this increment."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 90.0
  }
}
```

